    "narrative": "For this August 9th slate, **Corbin Carroll** (71.87) and **Mickey Moniak** (71.22) anchor our offensive production as our two elite-tier starts. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Wrobleski, where the pitcher's slow delivery provides a massive boost to his stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our Roto strategy\u2014and his placement in the #2 hole ensures maximum plate appearances. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** faces a softer matchup in McGreevy; his 71.22 score is driven by a potent combination of a significant platoon advantage and a favorable SP skill profile, making him a prime candidate for a multi-hit game. **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) also earns a strong recommendation today, as he draws a highly favorable matchup against V\u00e1squez, whose 4.97 xERA allows for an elevated ceiling despite the neutral park factors.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Cole Young** (40.82), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Zach McKinstry**. While **Cole Young** possesses a strong #2 spot in the order and a favorable stolen base environment against Seymour\u2019s slow delivery, his raw projected output simply could not surpass the wind-aided upside provided to **Zach McKinstry**. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding the matchup against Schlittler; **Austin Riley** (43.54) finds himself in a marginal start territory, as his production is severely hampered by Schlittler\u2019s elite 2.91 xERA. We are also monitoring the availability of **James Wood** and **Trevor Story**, who remain sidelined on the IL, while the rest of our depth, including **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte**, are being held in reserve to preserve our remaining game caps for more optimal matchups down the stretch.",
